  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 11
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Nightcycle #1018


    Ship maintenance records indicate damage to the
    following locations since the last cycle:


    Furnace Room

    Life Support

    Machine
    Room


    Survey the damage, finalize repairs, and return to cryosleep before
    the daycycle approaches. As required, the modules below outline information regarding
    your repairs and general ship traversal. Be sure to thoroughly read the module,
    the project board will not support new cohorts with our losses as they are currently.
    Meaning, if you die before another cohort is deployed, our research will be all
    for not.


    In front of you is a holographic map of the ship, the layout has
    been altered since your last thaw event. Familiarize yourself. Moving on; you
    will Interact [E] with installations around the ship, as you have with this Datapad.
    Repairs may include physically moving objects, though you should understand that
    given your title. Furthermore, other tasks may require a bit of intuition; hopefully
    that won''t be difficult for you.


    As stated, remain on task and do not
    waste time. You knew the risks coming to Project I.O.T.A., hold yourself to the
    standards expected and do your job. '
