MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1311366181}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 11
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1.1
  m_Text: 'Key Code: 4


    As you know, the purpose of Project I.O.T.A. is to study
    the atmospheric conditions of gas giants local to our galaxy. These gas giants
    possess the capability to transform into new stars, producing environmental effects
    to our galaxy that we do not yet understand. In the attempt to predict outcomes
    from when the giants begin their star events, your employer minted Project I.O.T.A.
    to commence building the Inverse Orbital Trajectory Apparatus. This apparatus,
    the one you''re currently residing in above 6D Alpha Infernus, operates on a
    furnace fueled neutral buoyancy system within the atmosphere. In order to maintain
    this bouyancy, the furnace must continue to pass routine inspection, else the
    ship is lost to the fumes of its current host giant.


    Part of your assignment
    as maintenance crew is to ensure sustained buoyancy, and with that comes challenges.
    A known weakness of the current iteration in your I.O.T.A. is the instability
    of components in the nodes of the furnace. These components, while designed to
    be sturdy, have the tendency to require realignment after  regular eruptions
    from chain events in the host giant atmosphere.


    Realign the components
    in the furnace nodes or risk losing the entire habitat. Follow the colors.'
--- !u!222 &1311366184
